name:           memcache
version:        0.4.0.0
x-revision:     1
synopsis:       A memcached client library.
description:    A client library for a Memcached cluster. Memcached is an in-memory key-value
                store typically used as a distributed and shared cache. Clients connect to a
                group of Memcached servers and perform out-of-band caching for things like
                SQL results, rendered pages, or third-party APIs.
                .
                It uses the Memcached Meta Text protocol and requires memcached 1.6.0 or
                newer. Username/password authentication is supported through memcached's
                @-Y authfile@ mode; the binary protocol and SASL authentication are no longer
                supported. It supports connecting to a single, or a cluster of Memcached
                servers. When connecting to a cluster, consistent hashing is used for routing
                requests to the appropriate server. Timeouts, retrying failed operations, and
                failover to a different server are all supported, as is Amazon ElastiCache
                auto discovery.
                .
                Multi-get is supported through the pipelined @getMany@. Keys containing
                whitespace or control bytes are sent using the protocol's base64 binary-key
                mode.
                .
                Basic usage is:
                .
                > import qualified Database.Memcache.Client as M
                >
                > mc <- M.newClient [M.ServerSpec "localhost" "11211" M.NoAuth] M.def
                > M.set mc "key" "value" 0 0
                > v <- M.get mc "key"
                .
                You should only need to import 'Database.Memcache.Client', but other modules
                are exposed for lower-level use. Version 0.4 is a breaking change from 0.3;
                see the changelog for details.
